msgctxt "button: make a copy"
msgid "Duplicate"
msgstr "Duplikálás"

#. translators: Link on the post editing screen that opens the setting for
#. translating drafts automatically. %1$s: the opening tag of the link, %2$s:
#. its closing tag.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:453
#, php-format
msgid "%1$sEnable automatic translation for drafts%2$s"
msgstr "%1$sVázlatok automatikus fordításának bekapcsolása%2$s"

#. translators: Link text on the post editing screen that folds the list of
#. translations away. It sits in brackets after the list and starts in lower
#. case. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:471
#: sitepress.class.php:3430
msgid "hide"
msgstr "elrejtés"

#. translators: Link text on the post editing screen that unfolds the list of
#. translations. It sits in brackets after the list and starts in lower case.
#. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:471
#: sitepress.class.php:3435
msgid "show"
msgstr "megjelenítés"

#. translators: Word shown in brackets after a language name in the
#. translations table of the post editing screen, marking a translation that
#. WPML keeps as a copy of the original. Noun.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:506
msgid "duplicate"
msgstr "duplikálás"

#. translators: First option in the dropdown that picks the original post this
#. one is a translation of: no post chosen. The dashes keep it apart from the
#. post titles.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:529
#: menu/wpml-translation-selector.class.php:40
#: menu/wpml-translation-selector.class.php:52
msgid "--None--"
msgstr "--Nincs--"

#. translators: Name of the checkbox that makes a copy of the post in another
#. language, used as its tooltip and, with the language name, as its screen
#. reader name. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:574
msgid "Create duplicate"
msgstr "Duplikátum létrehozása"

#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:582
msgid "This post is already duplicated."
msgstr "Ez a bejegyzés már duplikálva van."

#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:584
msgid "Can't create a duplicate. A translation is in progress."
msgstr "Nem hozható létre duplikátum. Fordítás van folyamatban."

#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:595
msgid "You don't have the rights to duplicate to this language."
msgstr "Nincs jogosultságod arra, hogy erre a nyelvre duplikálj."

#. translators: Screen reader label of a duplicate checkbox on the post
#. editing screen, e.g. "Create duplicate for German". %1$s: what the checkbox
#. does, or why it is disabled, %2$s: language name.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:602
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s for %2$s"
msgstr "A(z) %2$s esetén: %1$s"

#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:634
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:894
msgid "Post without a title"
msgstr "Cím nélküli bejegyzés"

#. translators: Heading of the media options in the WPML panel of the post
#. editing screen, on an original or a new post. Under it are two checkboxes:
#. "Featured image" and "Media attachments".
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:743
msgid "Use the same media in translations"
msgstr "Ugyanazon médiafájlok használata a fordításokban"

#. translators: Tooltip of the media options in the WPML panel of the post
#. editing screen, on an original or a new post. The items are the "Featured
#. image" and "Media attachments" checkboxes. %s: a link to the documentation,
#. already wrapped in its tags, whose text is "Learn more about translating
#. media with WPML".
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:745
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Translations reuse the checked items from this content. Uncheck an item to "
"use different media in translations. %s"
msgstr "A fordítások a tartalom bejelölt tételeit használják fel. Töröld egy tétel bejelölését, ha más médiafájlokat szeretnél használni a fordításokban. %s"

#. translators: Heading of the media options in the WPML panel of the post
#. editing screen, on a translation. Under it are two checkboxes: "Featured
#. image" and "Media attachments".
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:748
msgid "Use the same media as the original"
msgstr "Az eredetivel megegyező médiafájlok használata"

#. translators: Tooltip of the media options in the WPML panel of the post
#. editing screen, on a translation. The items are the "Featured image" and
#. "Media attachments" checkboxes. %s: a link to the documentation, already
#. wrapped in its tags, whose text is "Learn more about translating media with
#. WPML".
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:750
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This translation reuses the checked items from the original. Uncheck an item"
" to use different media in this translation. %s"
msgstr "Ez a fordítás az eredeti bejelölt tételeit használja fel. Töröld egy tétel bejelölését, ha más médiafájlokat szeretnél használni ebben a fordításban. %s"

#. translators: Checkbox under the media options heading in the WPML panel of
#. the post editing screen. Checked, the translations use the same featured
#. image.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:771
msgid "Featured image"
msgstr "Kiemelt kép"

#. translators: Checkbox under the media options heading in the WPML panel of
#. the post editing screen. Checked, the translations use the same images and
#. files attached to the content.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:773
msgid "Media attachments"
msgstr "Médiacsatolmányok"

#. translators: Button label on the post editing screen: bring the text of the
#. original language into this translation. %s: the name of the original
#. language.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:796
#, php-format
msgid "Copy content from %s"
msgstr "Tartalom másolása innen: %s"

#. translators: Tooltip of the button that copies the text of the original
#. language into this translation, on the post editing screen. "It" is that
#. button.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:804
msgid ""
"This operation copies the content from the original language onto this "
"translation. It's meant for when you want to start with the original "
"content, but keep translating in this language. This button is only enabled "
"when there's no content in the editor."
msgstr "Ez a művelet átmásolja az eredeti nyelvű tartalmat ebbe a fordításba. Akkor használd, ha az eredeti tartalommal szeretnéd kezdeni a munkát, de ezen a nyelven szeretnéd folytatni a fordítást. Ez a gomb csak akkor van bekapcsolva, ha a szerkesztőben nincs tartalom."

#. translators: Button label on the post editing screen: replace the text of
#. this translation with the text of the original language. %s: the name of
#. the original language.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:819
#, php-format
msgid "Overwrite with %s content."
msgstr "Felülírás a következő tartalmával: %s."

#. translators: Question asked before the text of a translation is replaced
#. with the text of the original language. %1$s: the name of the content type,
#. for example post or page, %2$s: the name of the original language.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:828
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The current content of this %1$s will be permanently lost. WPML will copy "
"the %2$s content and replace the current content."
msgstr "Az aktuális tartalom (%1$s) véglegesen elvész. A WPML átmásolja a tartalmat (%2$s), és lecseréli vele az aktuális tartalmat."

#. translators: Tooltip of the button that keeps this translation the same as
#. the original, on the post editing screen. "It" is that button.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-meta-boxes-post-edit-html.class.php:839
msgid ""
"This operation will synchronize this translation with the original language."
" When you edit the original, this translation will update immediately. It's "
"meant when you want the content in this language to always be the same as "
"the content in the original language."
msgstr "Ez a művelet szinkronizálja ezt a fordítást az eredeti nyelvvel. Ha szerkeszted az eredetit, ez a fordítás azonnal frissül. Akkor használd, ha azt szeretnéd, hogy ezen a nyelven a tartalom mindig megegyezzen az eredeti nyelvű tartalommal."

#. translators: Note on the post editing screen about fields WPML fills from
#. the original. %1$s: the names of those fields, in bold and separated by
#. commas, %2$s: the name of the original language.
#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-sync-custom-field-note.class.php:21
#, php-format
msgid "WPML will copy %1$s from %2$s when you save this post."
msgstr "A WPML a bejegyzés mentésekor átmásolja a következőt: %1$s. Forrás: %2$s."

#: menu/post-menus/post-edit-screen/wpml-sync-custom-field-note.class.php:25
msgid "Never show this"
msgstr "Ennek végleges elrejtése"

#. translators: Word shown next to a language in the list of the post editing
#. screen when that language is no longer used on the site. Past participle
#. used as a state.
#: menu/post-menus/wpml-post-language-filter.class.php:39
msgid "Removed"
msgstr "Eltávolítva"

#: menu/post-menus/wpml-post-language-filter.class.php:41
msgid "Languages that are off the site and still have content"
msgstr "A webhelyen nem használt, de tartalommal rendelkező nyelvek"

#. translators: Line on the Support screen. %1$s: the opening tag of a link to
#. the WPML support pages, %2$s: its closing tag.
#: menu/support.php:25
#, php-format
msgid "Technical support for clients is available via %1$sWPML support%2$s."
msgstr "Az ügyfelek technikai támogatása a %1$sWPML támogatásán%2$s keresztül érhető el."

#. translators: Column heading in the table of WPML plugins on the Support
#. screen.
#: menu/support.php:39
msgid "Plugin Name"
msgstr "Bővítmény neve"

#. translators: Value in the table of WPML plugins on the Support screen: the
#. plugin is not on this site. Past participle used as a state.
#: menu/support.php:58
msgid "Not installed"
msgstr "Nincs telepítve"

#. translators: Value in the table of WPML plugins on the Support screen: the
#. plugin is on this site. Past participle used as a state.
#: menu/support.php:61
msgid "Installed"
msgstr "Telepítve"

#. translators: Line on the Support screen. %1$s: the opening tag of a link to
#. the debug information screen, %2$s: its closing tag. The words between them
#. are the name of that screen.
#: menu/support.php:84
#, php-format
msgid ""
"For retrieving debug information if asked by support person, use the "
"%1$sdebug information%2$s page."
msgstr "Ha a támogatás munkatársa kéri, a hibakeresési információkat a %1$shibakeresési információk%2$s oldalon találod."

#. translators: The filter on the taxonomy translation screen when only the
#. terms are filtered, e.g. "Show [all categories]". %1$s: dropdown that picks
#. which terms to show. Show is a verb, imperative.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:19
#, php-format
msgid "Show %1$s"
msgstr "Megjelenítés: %1$s"

#. translators: The filter on the taxonomy translation screen, e.g. "Show
#. [untranslated categories] in [any language]". %1$s: dropdown that picks
#. which terms to show, %2$s: language dropdown. Show is a verb, imperative.
#. Keep both placeholders; you can change their order.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:25
#, php-format
msgid "Show %1$s in %2$s"
msgstr "%1$s mutatása itt: %2$s"

#. translators: Accessible name of the dropdown on the taxonomy translation
#. screen that picks all terms or only the untranslated ones.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:30
msgid "Filter by translation status"
msgstr "Szűrés fordítási állapot szerint"

#. translators: Accessible name of the language dropdown on the taxonomy
#. translation screen.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:32
msgid "Filter by language"
msgstr "Szűrés nyelv szerint"

#. translators: First word of the filter option "untranslated categories" on
#. the taxonomy translation screen; the name of the taxonomy follows it.
#. Adjective: the terms that have no translation yet.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:34
msgid "untranslated"
msgstr "lefordítatlan"

#. translators: First word of the filter option "all categories" on the
#. taxonomy translation screen; the name of the taxonomy follows it.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:36
msgid "all"
msgstr "összes"

#. translators: First option in the language dropdown on the taxonomy
#. translation screen: do not filter by language.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:42
msgid "any language"
msgstr "bármelyik nyelv"

#. translators: Button label next to the filters on the taxonomy translation
#. screen: load the list again with the chosen filters. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:44
msgid "Refresh"
msgstr "Frissítés"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:45
msgid "Update Taxonomy Hierarchy"
msgstr "Osztályozási hierarchia frissítése"

#. translators: First option in the dropdown that picks a parent term on the
#. taxonomy translation screen, shown between dashes.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:49
msgid "select parent"
msgstr "szülő kiválasztása"

#. translators: Label in front of the dropdown that picks the taxonomy to work
#. on. The dropdown follows the colon, so keep the trailing space.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:51
msgid "Select the taxonomy to translate: "
msgstr "Válaszd ki a lefordítandó taxonómiát: "

#. translators: Heading of the term translation section on the taxonomy
#. translation screen. %1$s: the name of the taxonomy in the singular, for
#. example Category.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:53
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s Translation"
msgstr "%1$s fordítása"

#. translators: Tab label on the taxonomy translation screen: the view where
#. the term hierarchy of a language is made to match the original.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:55
msgid "Hierarchy Synchronization"
msgstr "Hierarchia szinkronizálása"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:58
msgid "Copy to all languages"
msgstr "Másolás minden nyelvre"

#. translators: Question asked before a term is copied into every other
#. language, on the taxonomy translation screen. %1$s: the name of the
#. original language.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:60
#, php-format
msgid "Copy this term from original: %1$s to all other languages?"
msgstr "Másolod ezt a kifejezést az eredeti nyelvről (%1$s) az összes többi nyelvre?"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:61
msgid "Overwrite existing translations"
msgstr "Meglévő fordítások felülírása"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:62
msgid "Will be removed"
msgstr "Eltávolításra kerül"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:63
msgid "Will be added"
msgstr "Hozzáadásra kerül"

#. translators: Word in front of the colour key under the hierarchy
#. synchronization table.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:65
msgid "Legend:"
msgstr "Jelmagyarázat:"

#. translators: Line above the hierarchy synchronization table. %1$s: a
#. dropdown where the user picks the language whose hierarchy is copied.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:67
#, php-format
msgid "Synchronize taxonomy hierarchy according to: %1$s language."
msgstr "Osztályozási hierarchia szinkronizálása a következő nyelv szerint: %1$s."

#. translators: Heading on the taxonomy translation screen for the language a
#. term is translated into.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:69
msgid "Target Language"
msgstr "Célnyelv"

#. translators: Title of the dialog where a single term is translated.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:71
msgid "Term translation"
msgstr "Kifejezés fordítása"

#. translators: Title of the dialog that shows a term in its original
#. language.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:73
msgid "Original term"
msgstr "Eredeti kifejezés"

#. translators: Title of the dialog where the name of a taxonomy is
#. translated. Noun phrase: the translation of a label, not an instruction to
#. label something.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:75
msgid "Label translation"
msgstr "Címke fordítása"

#. translators: Heading in the term translation dialog, followed by the flag
#. and the name of the original language.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:78
msgid "Original:"
msgstr "Eredeti:"

#. translators: Heading in the term translation dialog, followed by the flag
#. and the name of the language being translated into.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:80
msgid "Translation to:"
msgstr "Fordítás erre a nyelvre:"

#. translators: Label of the field holding the name of a term in the term
#. translation dialog. Noun.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:82
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Név"

#. translators: Label of the field holding the part of the address that stands
#. for a term, in the term translation dialog.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:84
msgid "Slug"
msgstr "Slug"

#. translators: Button label that confirms a dialog and carries out what it
#. asks about.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:88
#: sitepress.class.php:1902
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#. translators: Label of the field holding the singular name of a taxonomy in
#. the label translation dialog.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:92
msgid "Singular"
msgstr "Egyedi"

#. translators: Label of the field holding the plural name of a taxonomy in
#. the label translation dialog.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:94
msgid "Plural"
msgstr "Többes szám"

#. translators: Link in a term row on the taxonomy translation screen that
#. opens the list of languages, so the term can be moved to another language.
#. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:96
msgid "Change language"
msgstr "Nyelv megváltoztatása"

#. translators: Text shown while the taxonomy translation screen is waiting
#. for data.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:100
msgid "loading"
msgstr "betöltés"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:105
msgid "Go to previous page"
msgstr "Ugrás az előző oldalra"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:106
msgid "Go to the next page"
msgstr "Lépj a következő oldalra"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:107
msgid "Go to the first page"
msgstr "Ugrás az első oldalra"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:108
msgid "Go to the last page"
msgstr "Ugrás az utolsó oldalra"

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:109
msgid "The taxonomy hierarchy is now synchronized."
msgstr "Az osztályozási hierarchia szinkronizálása megtörtént."

#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:110
msgid "The taxonomy hierarchy is already synchronized."
msgstr "Az osztályozási hierarchia már szinkronizálva van."

#. translators: Message shown instead of the table when no term matches the
#. filters. %1$s: the name of the taxonomy in the plural, for example
#. categories.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:112
#, php-format
msgid "No %1$s found."
msgstr "Nem található %1$s."

#. translators: Word after the number of terms under the table on the taxonomy
#. translation screen, as in "25 items". Plural.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:114
msgid "items"
msgstr "elemek"

#. translators: Heading of the term translation section on the taxonomy
#. translation screen. %1$s: the name of the taxonomy in the plural, in bold,
#. for example Categories.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:118
#, php-format
msgid "Translation of %1$s"
msgstr "%1$s fordítása"

#. translators: Heading of the section where the name and the address part of
#. a taxonomy are translated. %1$s: the name of the taxonomy in the singular,
#. in bold, for example Category.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:120
#, php-format
msgid "Translations of taxonomy %1$s labels and slug"
msgstr "%1$s taxonómia címkéinek és slugjának fordítása"

#. translators: Notice shown when the plugin that translates taxonomy names is
#. missing. %s: a link, already wrapped in its tags, whose text is the name of
#. that plugin.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:122
#, php-format
msgid "To translate taxonomy labels and slug you need %s plugin."
msgstr "Az osztályozási címkék és a slug fordításához szükséged van a %s bővítményre."

#. translators: Text shown while the taxonomy translation screen is waiting
#. for the terms.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:124
msgid "Loading ..."
msgstr "Betöltés ..."

#. translators: Error notice on the taxonomy translation screen when the list
#. of terms could not be loaded.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:126
msgid "The terms could not load. Reload the page to try again."
msgstr "Nem sikerült betölteni a kifejezéseket. Töltsd újra az oldalt az újrapróbálkozáshoz."

#. translators: Heading of the first column of the term table, holding the
#. terms as they are written in the original language. %1$s: the name of the
#. taxonomy in the singular, for example Category.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:128
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s terms (in original language)"
msgstr "%1$s kifejezés (eredeti nyelven)"

#. translators: Name of the plus icon in a term row on the taxonomy
#. translation screen, used as its tooltip and its screen reader name; the
#. language name comes before it. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:135
msgid "Add translation"
msgstr "Fordítás hozzáadása"

#. translators: Name of the pencil icon that opens a translation for editing,
#. used as its tooltip and its screen reader name. Verb, imperative.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:137
msgid "Edit translation"
msgstr "Fordítás szerkesztése"

#. translators: Tooltip and screen reader name of the spinning status icon
#. while WPML checks whether a translation is done; the language name comes
#. before it.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:139
msgid "Refreshing translation status. Please wait."
msgstr "Fordítási állapot frissítése. Kérlek, várj."

#. translators: Name of the icon that marks the language a term was written
#. in, used as its tooltip and its screen reader name; the language name comes
#. before it.
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:143
msgid "Original language"
msgstr "Eredeti nyelv"

#. translators: Name of the edit icon in a term row on the taxonomy
#. translation screen, used as its tooltip and its screen reader name. %1$s:
#. the language name, %2$s: the translated term, for example "Edit the German
#. translation: Bücher".
#: menu/term-taxonomy-menus/taxonomy-translation-display.class.php:152
#, php-format
msgid "Edit the %1$s translation: %2$s"
msgstr "%1$s fordítás szerkesztése: %2$s"

#. translators: Name of the icon that marks a term whose translation is out of
